# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Folio - environment
#
# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# Everything here is read in exactly one place: packages/db/src/env.ts. It is
# parsed once, through Zod, at import, and a missing or malformed value throws
# with the variable's name and where to get it. Nothing else in the repository
# reads process.env - eslint.config.mjs makes that an error, and
# packages/script cannot reach it at all, because AGENTS.md's purity rule bans
# `process` there outright.
#
# This file lists what THIS PHASE needs. Redis, Anthropic and Dodo are not here
# because no code reads them yet; adding one is a change to env.ts and to this
# file, together.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------


# =============================================================================
# SERVER ONLY - these must never reach the browser
#
# No NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix on any of them. That prefix is an instruction to
# Next.js to inline the value into client JavaScript, so a secret carrying it is
# a secret published on the first build. env.ts refuses any server variable
# whose name starts with it.
#
# On Railway these go in the service's variables. Never in a file that is
# committed, never in a client component, never in a log line.
# =============================================================================

# The SESSION pooler. One backend connection for its lifetime, so prepared
# statements, advisory locks and LISTEN/NOTIFY all work.
#
#   Used by: the worker, and every drizzle-kit migration.
#   From:    Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > Database >
#            Connection string > "Session pooler"
#
# Substitute your database password for [YOUR-PASSWORD]. If the password has
# any of @ : / ? # [ ] in it, percent-encode them or the URL will not parse.
DATABASE_URL_SESSION="postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:5432/postgres"

# The TRANSACTION pooler, port 6543. A different backend per transaction, which
# is why the client sets `prepare: false` - see packages/db/src/client.ts. Left
# preparing, it fails under load and not in development.
#
#   Used by: web requests.
#   From:    Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > Database >
#            Connection string > "Transaction pooler"
DATABASE_URL_TRANSACTION="postgresql://postgres.[PROJECT-REF]:[YOUR-PASSWORD]@aws-0-[REGION].pooler.supabase.com:6543/postgres"

# The service-role key. THE MOST DANGEROUS VALUE IN THIS FILE.
#
# It bypasses Row Level Security entirely. Anyone holding it can read and write
# every row of every project in the database. AGENTS.md, Tenancy: "The
# service-role key must never reach the browser."
#
# It is what makes the project-scoped repository layer the mechanism rather than
# a suggestion - there is no RLS underneath the server to catch a query that
# forgot its WHERE, which is why that is enforced in the type system instead.
#
#   Used by: Supabase Auth and Storage on the server. No data access - that is
#            Drizzle over the two URLs above.
#   From:    Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys > service_role
#
# If this ever appears in a browser bundle, a log, a screenshot or a support
# ticket: rotate it in the dashboard immediately. Rotating is cheap. Not
# rotating is total.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY="[SERVICE-ROLE-KEY]"


# =============================================================================
# SAFE TO EXPOSE - these are compiled into client JavaScript
#
# Both are designed to be public. The anon key is a JWT that carries no
# privilege on its own; RLS is what makes it safe, which is one reason the
# policies in migrations/0001_rls_and_grants.sql exist even though the server
# does not rely on them.
#
# Nothing in this phase reads these. They are declared now so the split between
# secret and public is written down before anything depends on it.
# =============================================================================

# The project's API URL.
#   From: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API > Project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL="https://[PROJECT-REF].supabase.co"

# The anon / publishable key.
#   From: Supabase dashboard > Project Settings > API Keys > anon (publishable)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY="[ANON-KEY]"


# =============================================================================
# Deliberately absent
#
# REDIS_URL           BullMQ. No queue yet - apps/worker is still a stub.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY   No agent yet.
# DODO_*              No payments yet, and AGENTS.md, When to ask first puts
#                     "anything Dodo" behind a question.
#
# Each arrives with the phase that reads it, added to env.ts and to this file in
# the same change. A variable that nothing reads is a variable nobody notices is
# wrong.
# =============================================================================
